title: Scope Constraint Parse Gating
story: friendly-zoo
description: ADR-271 acceptance 1 (via ADR-273) — the reachable scope constraint on petting is enforced at parse time. From the entrance the goats are out of scope and the command is refused by the parser; the identical command in the Petting Zoo dispatches to the pettable trait.
---

# The goats live in the Petting Zoo. From the entrance they are out of
# scope, so the must-be-reachable gate refuses the command at parse time.
> pet the goats
[OK: contains "can't see any such thing"]

# Articles gate identically to bare references (ADR-273 article handling).
> pet goats
[OK: contains "can't see any such thing"]

# Walk to where the goats are reachable.
> south
[OK: contains "gravel path"]
> east
[OK: contains "warm hay"]

# The same command now parses, passes the scope gate, and dispatches.
> pet the goats
[OK: contains "leans into your hand and bleats happily"]
